<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index rose to 1,434.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index rose to 1,434.</headline>
<text>
<p>LONDON, Dec 3 , Reuter - The Baltic Freight Index for spot dry cargo shipping rates rose to 1,434 today from 1,427 on Dec 2 , with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals 1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates in dollars per tonne.</p>
<p> Route			   Index    Rate    Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1   US GULF/ARA	  1464    13.294    1446    13.129</p>
<p>   1a  TRANSATLANTIC RV   1426 10800.000    1399 10593.000</p>
<p>   2   US GULF/JAPAN	1667    23.813    1657    23.679</p>
<p>   2a  SKAW P/USG/F EAST  1698 13925.000    1701 13950.000</p>
<p>   3   NOPAC/JAPAN	  1667    15.381    1660    15.314</p>
<p>   3a  JAPAN-SK/NOPAC/RV  1543 12175.000    1528 12057.000</p>
<p>   6   HR OR HR-RB/JAPAN  1213    12.506    1213    12.506</p>
<p>   7   HR/ROTTERDAM	 1231     5.994    1235     6.013</p>
<p>   8   QLAND/ROTTERDAM    0879     9.669    0880     9.681</p>
<p>   9   FE/NOPAC/SKAW-P    0916  8006.000    0911  7964.000</p>
<p>  10   TUBARAO/ROTTERDAM  1109     5.600    1110     5.606</p>
